WEBVTT

﻿1

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.337
Poets.


00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.036
Geniuses.


00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.750
LEMONADE MOUTH


00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:17.512
Revolutionaries.


00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:28.058
Lemonade Mouth has been called
all of these things.


00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:58.055
But the real story,
the story of how our band came to be,


00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:02.324
is a mystery to them all.


00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.730
I wonder if they'd believe it


00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.402
if I told them that it all started...


00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.276
Ooh, yeah


00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:22.745
Mm


00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:23.940
Breakthrough


00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.018
...right here.


00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.950
The rules in here are simple.


00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:32.616
No eating, no drinking, no sleeping,
no talking, no tapping, no texting.


00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:35.853
You break a rule,
l add another day of detention.


00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.896
Are we clear? Great.


00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:41.865
Stella Yamada, lead guitar.


00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.526
Wen Gifford, keyboard.


00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:47.139
Mo Banjaree, bass.


00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:50.265
Charlie Delgado, drum god.


00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:55.109
And me, Olivia White,
future frontman for Lemonade Mouth.


00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:58.116
One, two, three, four, five.


00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:05.786
It was this ragtag group of five
that started it all.


00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:11.388
All right. I have decided,


00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:15.592
rather than let you twiddle
your little thumbs for the next hour,


00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:19.068
we are going to
put those thumbs to use.


00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.298
We're gonna clean up around here.


00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:25.844
We're gonna unpack,
and we're gonna turn this storage room


00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:27.446
into a music room.


00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:32.250
I mean, we might as well
make the best of it, right?


00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:34.448
We've been banished to the basement.


00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.817
Did you hear that?


00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:42.792
Ooh.


00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:45.894
You know what?


00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:50.196
If they spent a fraction
of what that new gymnasium cost


00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.894
to keep this music program alive, I--


00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:56.640
Ooh.


00:02:57.844 --> 00:03:00.472
That is it. That is it.


00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:03.395
But if I'm gonna tell you this right,


00:03:04.051 --> 00:03:06.017
I need to go back to the beginning.


00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:08.347
The morning it all began.


00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:20.964
Let's go, Stell.


00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:25.831
You don't wanna be late
for your first day, do you?


00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:46.823
Look, I know this is hard.


00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:51.095
Transferring to a new school
a month into the year?


00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:52.562
Yeah. Yeah.


00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:00.130
Why would that be hard?


00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:01.900
Stella.


00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:04.700
Stella.


00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:08.606
- But who cares, right?
- I care.


00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:10.841
Then you and Dad
might have thought to ask me


00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:13.248
before you moved our family
halfway across the country.


00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:18.724
Hold that thought.


00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:23.819
Hello? Yes, Mr. Johnson.


00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:26.961
The bioplastic certification documents,
they should be on your desk...


00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.295
Ho-ho, check out the new girl.


00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:32.468
Nice hair.


00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:37.767
Have fun.


00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:45.372
Hey, Dad,
don't you think it's a little weird


00:04:45.373 --> 00:04:46.975
that your girlfriend's still in college?


00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:51.779
She's 28, Wen.
She's just taking a photography course.


00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:57.259
Look, Dad, when guys
go through midlife crisis, they--


00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:59.388
They buy a sports car, right?


00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:02.257
What do you say?
We turn in the truck, get a sports car?


00:05:02.258 --> 00:05:03.662
I would fully support that.


00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:09.000
Give Sydney a chance, for me.


00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:11.633
Why is everything about Sydney?


00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:16.641
"Sydney wants Chinese food."
"Let's watch Sydney's favorite show."


00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:19.343
"Can't pick you up from piano practice,
Sydney called."


00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:22.784
- Hey, I apologized for that.
- Yeah, I know.


00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:24.549
You know, whatever. Let's just go.


00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:27.216
I'm gonna be late
for my history presentation.


00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:42.840
Sorry.


00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:44.533
Are you excited, Charles?


00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.878
- Soccer tryouts are today.
- Oh.


00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:53.042
Right. Yeah, I'm-- I'm thrilled.


00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:55.381
- Oh, your mother--
- We.


00:05:55.855 --> 00:06:00.258
--thought you might like to have this
with you today, for luck.


00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:02.784
It was your brother's.


00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:07.591
Tommy scored the winning goal
at state finals with that ball.


00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:16.004
Mom, what are you crying for?
Tommy's just away at college.


00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.206
I... Oh.


00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:35.118
Whoa. Unh.


00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:39.498
Remember, Mohini, you need to speak
to your teachers about extra credit.


00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:42.226
Get your GPA up
for the college applications.


00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:44.995
But that's a couple of years away yet.


00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:48.335
It's never too soon to think about
your future, Monu. Understand?


00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:49.668
- Yes, Baba.
- Mm.


00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.371
Is that...?


00:06:52.779 --> 00:06:54.337
Is that lipstick you're wearing?


00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.375
No, Baba.


00:06:56.649 --> 00:07:00.278
Because you're too young
for that sort of thing.


00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:03.048
Yes, Baba. I'm late. Um...


00:07:03.456 --> 00:07:05.856
- Bye, Baba.
- Monu--


00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:08.324
Don't forget, extra credit.


00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:15.567
Please don't see me.
Please don't see me.


00:07:16.402 --> 00:07:17.562
Yeah, you know it.


00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:22.999
Have fun.


00:07:30.817 --> 00:07:32.944
Way to go, Olivia.


00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:58.000
One last reminder to
show some school spirit this weekend...


00:07:58.144 --> 00:08:00.112
Hey. There you are.


00:08:00.246 --> 00:08:01.770
Hey, Scott. You scared me.


00:08:01.914 --> 00:08:04.144
Well, I've been looking all over for you.


00:08:04.283 --> 00:08:08.413
So the band and I,
we're gonna ditch this morning,


00:08:08.554 --> 00:08:11.489
head on over to Ray's
and practice for the Halloween Bash.


00:08:11.624 --> 00:08:14.787
- Wanna come?
- Sure, I'd love--


00:08:15.528 --> 00:08:16.586
I can't.


00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:20.165
What? Come on, Mo.
We barely see each other as it is.


00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:21.731
Well, maybe this Saturday.


00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:23.860
I'll tell my dad
that I've got extra credit, or--


00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:27.439
No, you know I got Mudslide Crush
rehearsals all weekend,


00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:29.632
plus soccer practice.


00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:34.439
Come on. Just this once? For me?


00:08:35.114 --> 00:08:38.515
Don't worry about Brenigan, all right?
He's with the new girl.


00:08:42.789 --> 00:08:44.208
Well, I think that Stella's 


00:08:44.211 --> 00:08:46.755
still working through some anger issues
about moving.


00:08:46.893 --> 00:08:48.622
Yes, I can see that.


00:08:49.228 --> 00:08:51.822
But I'm afraid that shirt is...


00:08:51.964 --> 00:08:53.795
What?


00:08:53.933 --> 00:08:55.230
Is there a dress code here?


00:08:55.368 --> 00:08:59.634
Well, heh, no,
but there is an unwritten line,


00:08:59.772 --> 00:09:02.138
and that shirt crosses it.


00:09:03.843 --> 00:09:07.973
What about freedom of expression?
Do you have that here?


00:09:08.114 --> 00:09:13.017
Stella, just...cover up for the day, okay?


00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:21.918
Stella, is it?


00:09:23.296 --> 00:09:25.696
l run a tight ship here.


00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:28.322
I don't know how they did things
back in Rhode lsland,


00:09:28.467 --> 00:09:34.337
but in my school,
students respect the rules.


00:09:34.707 --> 00:09:39.440
Written...and unwritten.


00:09:48.354 --> 00:09:49.685
Come on, come on.


00:09:53.626 --> 00:09:56.720
Please don't call my dad. He doesn't
even want me alone with a boy.


00:09:56.862 --> 00:09:58.753
If he found out I skipped class with one,


00:09:58.765 --> 00:10:01.196
he'd never let me out of the house.


00:10:03.769 --> 00:10:06.067
This is your first infraction.


00:10:06.472 --> 00:10:08.531
You are on the honor roll.


00:10:11.243 --> 00:10:13.609
- I won't call your father.
- Thank you.


00:10:13.746 --> 00:10:15.373
This time.


00:10:16.015 --> 00:10:19.416
But if I ever catch you
skipping class again...


00:10:19.552 --> 00:10:21.042
You won't, I promise.


00:10:23.522 --> 00:10:27.117
That's why the American Revolution
was so important.


00:10:27.259 --> 00:10:29.124
Thank you, Sharon. Very nice.


00:10:29.996 --> 00:10:31.122
All right.


00:10:32.665 --> 00:10:35.828
Wendell, you're up.


00:10:48.981 --> 00:10:50.448
What?


00:10:51.183 --> 00:10:54.175
- We're waiting.
- One second, sir.


00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:55.617
I'm sorry.


00:10:55.755 --> 00:10:57.746
Sorry. Um...


00:11:00.092 --> 00:11:02.526
This can't be happening.


00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:07.631
Hi. I'm sorry to interrupt.


00:11:07.767 --> 00:11:10.361
Wen, I have your folder.


00:11:11.737 --> 00:11:12.863
Check out Wen's mommy.


00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:16.674
- You must be Wendell's mother.
- No, I'm--


00:11:16.809 --> 00:11:18.208
She's not my mom, okay?


00:11:18.344 --> 00:11:21.541
Are you kidding me? Look at her.
All right, are you stupid?


00:11:21.681 --> 00:11:23.342
- Whoa.
- Oh.


00:11:30.523 --> 00:11:32.684
- So...?
- Detention.


00:11:35.594 --> 00:11:38.586
But at least we'll be together, right?


00:11:40.266 --> 00:11:41.665
Right?


00:11:41.801 --> 00:11:45.293
No, he actually let me off
with a warning.


00:11:45.438 --> 00:11:47.030
- A warning?
- Yeah.


00:11:47.173 --> 00:11:50.404
You know, I got soccer practice,
some big games coming up.


00:11:50.543 --> 00:11:55.276
I just can't miss them.
But I'll see you at lunch, okay?


00:11:55.414 --> 00:11:57.974
- Yeah, sure.
- All right.


00:11:59.118 --> 00:12:01.177
Unbelievable.


00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:05.980
What can I tell you, Jenny?


00:12:06.125 --> 00:12:10.152
That you put the same value on the arts
as you do sports.


00:12:10.296 --> 00:12:12.423
You've cut the music budget to zero.


00:12:12.565 --> 00:12:15.261
You've moved my classroom
down to the basement.


00:12:15.401 --> 00:12:17.460
And for what? Some gymnasium?


00:12:17.603 --> 00:12:20.367
Whoa. This is not "some gymnasium."


00:12:20.506 --> 00:12:23.373
Sports bring donors, donors bring money,


00:12:23.509 --> 00:12:26.842
and money makes my school run.


00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:29.343
Your school?


00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:35.582
Times are tough, Jenny.


00:12:35.721 --> 00:12:40.522
Someone's gotta make the hard decisions
around here, and that someone is moi.


00:12:45.431 --> 00:12:50.232
"I'm Nobody. Who are you?
Are you nobody too?"


00:12:50.369 --> 00:12:52.530
Heh. Well, that would be a yes.


00:13:19.231 --> 00:13:21.426
Here we go, hustle up. Move it, move it.


00:13:21.567 --> 00:13:23.728
- Come on, let's make a move.
- Unh.


00:13:23.869 --> 00:13:26.099
- Heh.
- Ray, cut it out, dude.


00:13:26.572 --> 00:13:29.871
Keep it going. Keep it going.
Delgado, come on, get with the program.


00:13:30.009 --> 00:13:31.636
- I'll see you later.
- Eh.


00:13:31.811 --> 00:13:33.836
Come on, what are y'all doing?


00:13:36.348 --> 00:13:38.407
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Let's go, Delgado. Come on.


00:13:38.551 --> 00:13:41.247
All right, guys,
set up for drill number two. Hustle up.


00:13:41.387 --> 00:13:43.082
- Coach.
- Come on, kids.


00:13:43.222 --> 00:13:46.419
- Drill number two.
- Drill two, kids, come on.


00:13:48.561 --> 00:13:51.928
Are you sure
that's Tommy Delgado's brother?


00:13:52.064 --> 00:13:54.760
- Yeah.
- No, no, Delgado, you gotta kick the ball.


00:13:55.501 --> 00:13:56.661
Like...that.


00:13:58.537 --> 00:14:01.131
That's it. You know what?
I don't wanna play soccer,


00:14:01.273 --> 00:14:02.357
I don't want your abuse,


00:14:02.531 --> 00:14:04.504
and I certainly don't want my brother's ball.


00:14:05.845 --> 00:14:07.437
Ooh.


00:14:08.314 --> 00:14:11.044
Yeah, I think he did that on purpose,
coach.


00:14:18.524 --> 00:14:20.116
- Aah!
- TurboBlast.


00:14:26.532 --> 00:14:28.727
TurboBlast.


00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:38.068
Welcome to our first assembly
in our new gym,


00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:41.873
generously funded by our school sponsor,
TurboBlast.


00:14:42.014 --> 00:14:44.346
Drink of champions.


00:14:44.483 --> 00:14:45.973
Yeah. Whoo!


00:14:46.118 --> 00:14:48.552
You the man, Brenigan.


00:14:50.456 --> 00:14:53.516
Right there, that. That's good, Phil.
Thanks.


00:14:56.428 --> 00:14:59.420
Our assembly today is about--


00:15:00.165 --> 00:15:01.894
Are you ready?


00:15:02.635 --> 00:15:03.727
--personal empowerment.


00:15:03.869 --> 00:15:05.302
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:15:05.437 --> 00:15:07.997
That's right. Dig deep inside,
find the power within...


00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:10.665
Why don't you, uh, find another seat?


00:15:12.044 --> 00:15:13.909
- Why don't you make me?
- Oh!


00:15:14.346 --> 00:15:18.510
--excel not only on the field,
they excel in life.


00:15:18.651 --> 00:15:20.414
All right, move it.


00:15:21.086 --> 00:15:23.554
- Come on.
- What a freak.


00:15:23.689 --> 00:15:28.092
A student who's willing to take risks.


00:15:28.227 --> 00:15:30.388
An empowered student.


00:15:31.497 --> 00:15:36.264
And by empowerment, I mean going
above and beyond what's expected of you.


00:15:36.402 --> 00:15:38.199
You want empowered students?


00:15:38.337 --> 00:15:41.864
Now, I know it's all within you,
and you know it is as well.


00:15:42.007 --> 00:15:44.999
- Then you're gonna get them.
- On behalf of TurboBlast,


00:15:45.144 --> 00:15:46.441
all our coaches--


00:15:46.578 --> 00:15:49.479
My shirt, my decision. Okay?


00:15:49.615 --> 00:15:52.277
Don't let your school
take away your rights. Okay?


00:15:52.418 --> 00:15:55.046
Be heard. Use your voice.


00:15:57.623 --> 00:15:59.022
Come on.


00:15:59.158 --> 00:16:01.820
- He can't tell you what to wear, who to be.
- Let's go.


00:16:01.961 --> 00:16:03.622
You can wear what you want.


00:16:04.129 --> 00:16:06.927
We can wear whatever we want.


00:16:07.666 --> 00:16:09.099
- Whoo!
- Come on.


00:16:09.234 --> 00:16:10.326
Sit down.


00:16:10.469 --> 00:16:13.267
I can wear my own T-shirt.


00:16:13.405 --> 00:16:17.136
Wear whatever kind of shirt you want.
Today, tomorrow.


00:16:18.277 --> 00:16:20.108
Okay. Ready? Okay.


00:16:22.014 --> 00:16:23.948
Defense! Push 'em back!


00:16:24.083 --> 00:16:25.311
Defense! Push 'em back!


00:16:25.451 --> 00:16:29.080
Defense! Push 'em back! Way back!


00:16:29.221 --> 00:16:31.655
Defense! Push 'em back!


00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:43.031
You lost?


00:16:43.168 --> 00:16:46.535
- Oh, no, I'm just looking--
- Detention, huh? Follow me.


00:16:47.773 --> 00:16:52.267
- What is this place?
- This is the underground.


00:16:52.411 --> 00:16:55.141
Robotics club. Hey, Alex.
You working hard?


00:16:55.748 --> 00:16:57.739
Shakespeare society.


00:17:00.285 --> 00:17:03.379
Chess club.
He hasn't found a partner in months.


00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:06.455
Ballet.


00:17:06.592 --> 00:17:08.526
And one, and two...


00:17:09.628 --> 00:17:11.391
Mathletes.


00:17:12.164 --> 00:17:13.426
Art club.


00:17:13.565 --> 00:17:15.294
Looking good, honey


00:17:15.434 --> 00:17:16.662
Play that, DJ. What you say?


00:17:16.802 --> 00:17:20.636
Even the school newspaper.
Victoria, you doing good?


00:17:21.273 --> 00:17:23.298
Anything that doesn't fit
Principal Brenigan's mold,


00:17:23.442 --> 00:17:24.500
you'll find it down here.


00:17:25.844 --> 00:17:27.209
Oh. This is my stop, AV club.


00:17:27.613 --> 00:17:30.639
You're telling me Brenigan
just stuck your clubs in the basement?


00:17:31.083 --> 00:17:33.449
Pretty much.
Unless you're wearing a varsity jacket


00:17:33.585 --> 00:17:36.145
- or a cheer skirt, you're basically--
- Invisible.


00:17:36.288 --> 00:17:40.281
See? You're catching on already.
Detention's at the end of the hall.


00:17:40.426 --> 00:17:41.757
Good luck.


00:17:41.894 --> 00:17:44.692
No, guys. You keep doing this wrong.


00:17:57.209 --> 00:17:58.870
There is a moment


00:18:04.883 --> 00:18:07.374
where the stars align


00:18:10.756 --> 00:18:13.316
and fates collide,


00:18:16.261 --> 00:18:18.593
creating that perfect union.


00:18:22.167 --> 00:18:23.225
Mm. Hmm.


00:18:26.538 --> 00:18:29.234
This was that moment.


00:18:33.112 --> 00:18:35.910
I am gonna give Brenigan
a piece of my mind, and while I do,


00:18:36.048 --> 00:18:39.882
I want you guys to just start
cleaning up or something around here.


00:18:40.719 --> 00:18:41.913
She can't make us clean.


00:18:43.288 --> 00:18:47.315
- It's cruel and unusual punishment.
- Welcome to high school.


00:18:50.429 --> 00:18:52.397
This school stinks.


00:18:52.531 --> 00:18:55.625
Can you guys just do what Miss Reznick
asked and be quiet? Okay?


00:18:55.767 --> 00:18:59.203
I'm not getting another detention
because of you people.


00:19:58.163 --> 00:20:00.791
Na, na, na, na, na


00:20:00.933 --> 00:20:03.333
Na, na


00:20:03.468 --> 00:20:05.459
Take a look around


00:20:05.604 --> 00:20:08.198
Who would have thought
We'd all be here?


00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:11.138
So let's mess around


00:20:11.276 --> 00:20:13.335
'Cause the future is unclear


00:20:13.478 --> 00:20:15.969
We got nothing better to do


00:20:16.114 --> 00:20:18.912
We're just trying to get through


00:20:19.051 --> 00:20:21.417
