Like on a stage. I can't do that.


00:23:52.931 --> 00:23:55.058
Oh, come on. Sure you can.


00:23:55.200 --> 00:23:57.191
No, no, trust me, it wouldn't be pretty.


00:23:57.335 --> 00:23:59.769
The last time I performed on-stage
was my first-grade recital.


00:23:59.905 --> 00:24:01.175
Five minutes into "Baa, Baa, Black Sheep"


00:24:01.176 --> 00:24:02.999
I threw up down Mikey Nichols' back.


00:24:03.141 --> 00:24:05.939
Ha, ha. Yeah, I remember that.
That was hilarious.


00:24:06.077 --> 00:24:07.772
No, it was humiliating.


00:24:08.780 --> 00:24:10.270
I'm sorry, I can't.


00:24:11.216 --> 00:24:14.185
Well, I--
I guess that counts me out, right?


00:24:14.319 --> 00:24:17.186
Can't really enter a competition
with one man in a band.


00:24:17.322 --> 00:24:19.950
You know, unless you're thinking
of a solo career.


00:24:20.091 --> 00:24:21.422
Which I'd be happy to consider.


00:24:21.560 --> 00:24:25.826
Guys, Mudslide Crush are entering.
We wouldn't have a shot.


00:24:25.964 --> 00:24:27.591
He's right. They're amazing.


00:24:27.732 --> 00:24:29.131
They're not that amazing.


00:24:29.267 --> 00:24:32.430
Well, if we don't stand a chance
against these Mudslide guys,


00:24:32.571 --> 00:24:35.631
then why bother, right?


00:24:35.774 --> 00:24:38.709
Because, you said it yourself,


00:24:38.844 --> 00:24:41.904
you deserve to be heard.


00:25:06.404 --> 00:25:07.928
Gram?


00:25:09.441 --> 00:25:10.965
Gram.


00:25:11.409 --> 00:25:14.276
Hey. Oh, Olivia, sweetie.


00:25:14.412 --> 00:25:16.175
- Hey.
- Ha, ha. Aw.


00:25:16.715 --> 00:25:18.307
Oh, how's Nancy doing?


00:25:18.450 --> 00:25:20.816
Oh, she still hasn't eaten.


00:25:20.952 --> 00:25:25.048
Nance. Come here. You need to eat.


00:25:25.290 --> 00:25:26.882
You need to eat, old girl.


00:25:27.025 --> 00:25:30.859
Come on, girl. Come on. Look. Yum.


00:25:33.198 --> 00:25:34.290
Hey there, buddy.


00:25:34.432 --> 00:25:36.696
We're going out for a ride. Wanna come?


00:25:38.036 --> 00:25:39.469
No, I don't like to ride.


00:25:41.106 --> 00:25:43.700
- Yes, you do.
- No, I don't.


00:25:43.842 --> 00:25:47.243
Come on, Wen. Since when
don't you like to ride your horse?


00:25:56.354 --> 00:25:59.346
Come on, ladies.
We are going for a ride.


00:26:29.254 --> 00:26:30.949
Charlie!


00:26:36.962 --> 00:26:38.259
So?


00:26:40.198 --> 00:26:41.392
How were soccer tryouts?


00:26:42.767 --> 00:26:44.234
Well, um


00:26:44.369 --> 00:26:46.064
they were...


00:26:47.038 --> 00:26:49.097
- Great.
- Oh!


00:26:49.240 --> 00:26:53.176
- It went-- It went great.
- I knew it. I knew it. Mwah.


00:26:53.311 --> 00:26:55.575
Why don't you come in now
and hit the books?


00:26:55.714 --> 00:26:58.205
You're never gonna make it to Stanford
with your brother


00:26:58.350 --> 00:27:01.148
whacking away at these drums
every day, are you?


00:27:01.686 --> 00:27:04.086
Come on. Start with your math.


00:27:08.059 --> 00:27:09.959
Yuck, Dad.


00:27:10.428 --> 00:27:12.055
How can you eat that?


00:27:12.397 --> 00:27:14.661
Imagine how that poor fish felt.


00:27:15.233 --> 00:27:16.894
Fish don't feel pain.


00:27:18.370 --> 00:27:21.464
Just because you don't see agony
doesn't mean it's not there.


00:27:21.606 --> 00:27:24.131
When did you become a vegetarian?


00:27:24.275 --> 00:27:27.904
Yeah, when did, uh, this happen?


00:27:33.918 --> 00:27:35.283
Four months ago.


00:27:36.354 --> 00:27:38.413
For geniuses,
you don't pay very good attention.


00:27:40.225 --> 00:27:41.419
Because it's stupid, Stella.


00:27:41.793 --> 00:27:42.851
Timmy.


00:27:44.529 --> 00:27:48.021
Sorry I'm not out inventing
biodegradable plastic,


00:27:48.166 --> 00:27:53.433
or making my own toys, or,
oh, yeah, curing cancer.


00:27:53.938 --> 00:27:56.634
We haven't cured it yet, honey.


00:27:56.775 --> 00:28:00.108
Hello. I know that.


00:28:00.545 --> 00:28:01.671
l may not be a genius--


00:28:01.813 --> 00:28:05.476
Which is, like, I don't know,
a genetic abnormality in this family.


00:28:05.884 --> 00:28:08.318
But I can do things too, you know.


00:28:14.559 --> 00:28:17.995
I could start a revolution.


00:28:18.897 --> 00:28:21.127
That's nice, dear.


00:28:21.366 --> 00:28:25.063
Good morning, Mesa High.
Yes, it's that time of year again.


00:28:25.203 --> 00:28:27.535
You have to get out there and vote,
because guess what.


00:28:27.672 --> 00:28:31.039
Yes, I have been nominated, yet again,
for School Administrator of the Year.


00:28:31.176 --> 00:28:32.666
Let's keep that winning streak alive.


00:28:35.947 --> 00:28:37.574
Okay.


00:28:38.316 --> 00:28:41.752
Vote today, the polls are open all day.
There's extra credit involved.


00:28:57.168 --> 00:28:59.159
- You think it's about the band?
- Oh, my.


00:29:11.116 --> 00:29:12.913
We talked about this.
It's not gonna happen.


00:29:13.051 --> 00:29:14.416
Sure it is.


00:29:15.520 --> 00:29:17.750
l signed us up for Rising Star
this morning.


00:29:17.889 --> 00:29:19.720
Check. Check, one, two, check.


00:29:19.858 --> 00:29:21.587
We're not experienced enough.


00:29:21.726 --> 00:29:25.389
Which is why I also signed us up
for Halloween Bash.


00:29:26.731 --> 00:29:29.256
- Check, check, one, two, check.
- What?


00:29:29.400 --> 00:29:31.027
Wait, how'd you pull that off?


00:29:31.469 --> 00:29:33.306
It's amazing what a principal will agree to


00:29:33.358 --> 00:29:35.735
