00:29:35.874 --> 00:29:38.240
is channeling her energy
into something productive.


00:29:38.376 --> 00:29:39.434
Hmm.


00:29:39.577 --> 00:29:41.909
Goofing around in detention
does not make us a band.


00:29:42.046 --> 00:29:44.173
So we'll practice.


00:29:44.315 --> 00:29:46.374
You have real drums, right?


00:29:46.518 --> 00:29:48.543
- Yeah.
- See?


00:29:48.686 --> 00:29:51.382
- I didn't even know that.
- Ha, ha.


00:29:51.523 --> 00:29:53.150
Okay, so, what are we gonna play?


00:29:53.725 --> 00:29:55.056
You could write our songs.


00:29:55.193 --> 00:29:56.626
- Me?
- Yeah.


00:29:56.761 --> 00:30:00.094
That one you did the other day
was pretty amazing.


00:30:00.231 --> 00:30:02.597
- Mm-hm.
- That was nothing.


00:30:03.868 --> 00:30:04.960
I think I'm gonna be sick.


00:30:05.503 --> 00:30:08.666
Wait. We can't play the Bash.
Mudslide Crush is playing.


00:30:08.807 --> 00:30:11.867
And we are opening for them.


00:30:15.380 --> 00:30:17.644
I don't know about the rest of you guys,


00:30:17.782 --> 00:30:21.741
but I don't wanna be some random face
in a yearbook.


00:30:21.886 --> 00:30:25.413
Or a kid people vaguely recall
passing in the halls.


00:30:25.557 --> 00:30:27.491
I wanna be heard.


00:30:31.930 --> 00:30:33.397
- Hi.
- Ha, ha.


00:30:33.531 --> 00:30:37.467
Wen and I are in. Who's with us?


00:30:38.203 --> 00:30:39.864
I'll give it a shot.


00:30:40.572 --> 00:30:41.698
- Really?
- Yeah?


00:30:41.840 --> 00:30:43.933
But only if everyone else agrees.


00:30:44.676 --> 00:30:47.645
Just one practice. If it works, great.
If not, I'm out.


00:30:47.779 --> 00:30:49.747
- All right.
- Okay. Ha, ha.


00:30:51.149 --> 00:30:52.582
Hey.


00:30:52.717 --> 00:30:53.945
Mm-mm.


00:30:54.085 --> 00:30:57.612
Come on. Say you'll try.


00:30:57.755 --> 00:30:59.416
- Please.
- It'll be fun.


00:30:59.557 --> 00:31:00.615
It'll be so much fun.


00:31:00.758 --> 00:31:03.454
- Pretty please, sugar on top?
- You will have so much fun.


00:31:03.595 --> 00:31:05.859
D'oh. Okay, okay. I'll do it.


00:31:05.997 --> 00:31:09.626
- Yes. Yes.
- It'll be great.


00:31:14.105 --> 00:31:15.663
You know what?


00:31:16.574 --> 00:31:18.166
Heads, we do it.


00:31:19.177 --> 00:31:20.735
Tails, we don't.


00:31:24.616 --> 00:31:27.551
One of the misconceptions
about Lemonade Mouth


00:31:27.685 --> 00:31:29.448
is that we were a natural fit
from the start.


00:31:30.788 --> 00:31:32.449
Totally not true.


00:31:32.590 --> 00:31:35.582
Come on, Charlie.
It's a simple four-four beat.


00:31:35.960 --> 00:31:37.052
You're not even trying.


00:31:37.195 --> 00:31:42.861
It's B to B-flat, back to B,
then an F-sharp. Ready?


00:31:52.310 --> 00:31:53.937
Okay, this isn't working.


00:31:54.512 --> 00:31:57.572
We'll get it.
We just need to keep practicing.


00:31:57.715 --> 00:32:00.115
Also, maybe we need to go
a little more hardcore.


00:32:02.086 --> 00:32:04.281
That's it. I'm out of here.


00:32:04.856 --> 00:32:06.585
What? You're just gonna stomp away?


00:32:07.091 --> 00:32:08.217
Yeah, come on. Don't leave.


00:32:08.359 --> 00:32:11.385
In case you guys hadn't realized,
I'm classically trained.


00:32:11.529 --> 00:32:14.362
On the violin.
I don't play whatever this is.


00:32:16.935 --> 00:32:18.596
I'm-- I'm out too.


00:32:18.937 --> 00:32:20.495
- What?
- Guys, look.


00:32:20.638 --> 00:32:22.367
Come on. We can work this out.


00:32:22.507 --> 00:32:23.701
Yeah. Yeah, Wen's right.


00:32:23.841 --> 00:32:26.309
Maybe if we just take it from the top
one more time?


00:32:26.444 --> 00:32:28.605
They're quitting
before we've even started.


00:32:30.248 --> 00:32:31.772
- They're quitters!
- Shut up, Stella.


00:32:32.317 --> 00:32:33.750
- Wait, Mo.
- Mo.


00:32:33.885 --> 00:32:35.352
Please, don't. Wait.


00:32:46.564 --> 00:32:48.293
Can you see me?


00:32:49.434 --> 00:32:51.163
'Cause I'm right here


00:32:52.704 --> 00:32:54.433
Can you listen?


00:32:55.206 --> 00:32:57.606
'Cause I've been trying
To make you notice


00:32:58.009 --> 00:33:00.603
What it would mean to me


00:33:00.745 --> 00:33:03.305
To feel like somebody


00:33:04.082 --> 00:33:06.983
We've been on our way to nowhere


00:33:07.118 --> 00:33:09.746
Tryin' so hard to get there


00:33:09.887 --> 00:33:14.449
And I say
Oh, we're gonna let it show


00:33:14.959 --> 00:33:18.986
We're gonna just let go of everything


00:33:19.130 --> 00:33:21.826
Holding back our dreams


00:33:21.966 --> 00:33:25.663
And try to make it come alive


00:33:26.637 --> 00:33:30.596
Come on, let it shine so they can see


00:33:30.742 --> 00:33:33.802
We were meant to be


00:33:33.945 --> 00:33:36.379
- Somebody
- Somebody


00:33:36.514 --> 00:33:38.948
- Somebody, yeah
- Somebody


00:33:39.083 --> 00:33:43.782
Somehow, someday, some way


00:33:43.921 --> 00:33:46.446
- Boy, go to class.
- Somebody


00:33:46.591 --> 00:33:48.149
Get out of this darkness


00:33:48.292 --> 00:33:53.958
Feel the spotlight glowing
Like a yellow sun


00:33:54.098 --> 00:33:57.192
- Oh-ooh-oh, oh oh
- Oh-ooh-oh, oh oh


00:33:57.335 --> 00:33:59.826
And when we fall. We fall together


00:33:59.971 --> 00:34:05.637
Till we get back up
And we will rise as one


00:34:06.210 --> 00:34:07.939
Oh, oh


00:34:09.280 --> 00:34:12.215
Oh, oh, oh. We're gonna let it show


00:34:12.350 --> 00:34:17.185
- Let it show
- We're gonna just let go of everything


00:34:17.321 --> 00:34:19.983
Holding back our dreams


00:34:20.124 --> 00:34:23.560
- And try
- To make it come alive


00:34:23.694 --> 00:34:24.888
Make it come alive


00:34:25.029 --> 00:34:29.090
Come on, let it shine
So they can see


00:34:29.233 --> 00:34:31.861
We were meant to be


00:34:32.003 --> 00:34:33.903
Somebody


00:34:34.038 --> 00:34:36.836
Somebody
Somebody, yeah


00:34:36.974 --> 00:34:38.032
Somebody


00:34:38.176 --> 00:34:41.668
Somehow, someday, some way


00:34:42.814 --> 00:34:44.941
Somebody


00:34:47.985 --> 00:34:49.953
Olivia, did you really write that?


00:34:50.354 --> 00:34:51.787
Yeah. Ha, ha.


00:34:52.356 --> 00:34:53.948
You guys,


00:34:54.092 --> 00:34:56.287
we are so winning a record deal.


00:35:04.969 --> 00:35:08.962
So Brenigan took away half my set
for the Halloween Bash.


00:35:09.107 --> 00:35:11.371
- What?
- Yeah, I know. The guy's insane.


00:35:11.509 --> 00:35:15.445
I mean, what is he gonna do?
I mean, I'm the man, all right?


00:35:16.881 --> 00:35:20.715
Hey, what's up?
I didn't think you were gonna make it.


00:35:20.852 --> 00:35:23.252
So how'd you get out of the house?


00:35:23.387 --> 00:35:26.356
- Um, I told my dad I had a study group.
- Ha, ha.


00:35:26.491 --> 00:35:29.619
I mean-- I mean, what does Brenigan
expect me to do? Jump up and down?


00:35:29.760 --> 00:35:33.196
Like, "Oh, I get to play half my set?" No.


00:35:33.331 --> 00:35:36.926
- What's Ray talking about?
- Eh, it's nothing.


00:35:38.336 --> 00:35:40.736
- Come on, don't worry about it.
- Just tell me.


00:35:41.472 --> 00:35:44.930
Brenigan told us we don't get
the full set at the Halloween Bash.


00:35:46.177 --> 00:35:47.405
So...


00:35:47.545 --> 00:35:50.241
- So you know that new girl, Stella?
- Mm-hm.


00:35:50.681 --> 00:35:53.514
Yeah, well, I guess she told Brenigan
she has some band,


00:35:53.651 --> 00:35:55.278
and Miss Reznick is in on it.


00:35:55.953 --> 00:35:58.251
Miss Reznick is a really
talented music teacher, actually.


00:35:58.389 --> 00:36:00.414
Yeah, whatever.
I mean, that's not the point.


00:36:00.558 --> 00:36:05.393
The point is, this so-called band
has half our stage time now. It's nuts.


00:36:05.530 --> 00:36:06.929
You don't cancel the Crush.


00:36:07.064 --> 00:36:08.793
Um, do you know who else
is in the band?


00:36:08.933 --> 00:36:11.766
Nope. Just a bunch of nobodies.


00:36:12.236 --> 00:36:15.205
- Okay, and that's why--
- Hey, hey, get away from my car.


00:36:15.339 --> 00:36:18.274
- It's me.
- What?


00:36:18.409 --> 00:36:20.639
I'm in the band.


00:36:21.245 --> 00:36:22.439
I play bass.


00:36:25.850 --> 00:36:27.340
I mean, you're kidding, right?


00:36:27.685 --> 00:36:30.984
No. Actually, we're not bad.


00:36:31.122 --> 00:36:32.783
I mean, we met in detention.


00:36:35.993 --> 00:36:37.483
We're just opening for you.


00:36:37.628 --> 00:36:40.927
Look, Mo, I mean, if you wanna be
in the band, that's great.


00:36:41.065 --> 00:36:43.966
You could play backup guitar for me
or something.


00:36:44.101 --> 00:36:46.695
But, come on, joining a band
that's taking half our night from us?


00:36:46.837 --> 00:36:49.965
- What's up with that?
- What, so now it's your night?


00:36:50.107 --> 00:36:55.044
Yeah. I mean, my music, it's--
It's important to me. You know that.


00:36:55.179 --> 00:36:58.205
Well, maybe my music
is important to me too.


00:36:58.349 --> 00:37:01.682
I'm sure it is. It's just...


00:37:04.522 --> 00:37:05.887
Just think about it, okay?


00:37:06.557 --> 00:37:09.492
I mean, I really don't want this
to come between us.


00:37:10.661 --> 00:37:13.061
Me either. It's... Ahh.


00:37:13.197 --> 00:37:15.062
Good. Good.


00:37:15.866 --> 00:37:18.357
Now, I'll be back in a little bit, okay?


00:37:20.371 --> 00:37:23.363
I'm taking that band down
one way or another, okay?


00:37:23.507 --> 00:37:25.865
Ray. We're up, my man.


00:37:25.943 --> 00:37:28.605
- All right, let's do this thing. Let's do it.
- Yeah.


00:37:31.882 --> 00:37:33.076
Yeah, I love this song!


00:37:45.329 --> 00:37:47.524
Who's that trying to talk to me?


00:37:47.665 --> 00:37:50.429
Standing over there
Looking like a wannabe


00:37:50.568 --> 00:37:53.036
Keep me on ice, subzero degrees


00:37:53.371 --> 00:37:56.067
I'm so solid
That you can't see through me


00:37:56.207 --> 00:37:58.607
We rock the stage like a playoff game


00:37:58.743 --> 00:38:01.234
Don't have to say it. You know my name


00:38:01.379 --> 00:38:03.870
Three-point shot. No time on the clock


00:38:04.015 --> 00:38:05.949
And the crowd goes wild
Are you ready or not?


00:38:06.317 --> 00:38:07.784
Oh


00:38:08.386 --> 00:38:12.117
And the crowd goes
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh


00:38:12.256 --> 00:38:13.621
Oh, oh, oh, oh


00:38:13.758 --> 00:38:17.455
And the crowd goes
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh


00:38:17.595 --> 00:38:20.086
Oh, oh, oh, oh. And the crowd goes


00:38:20.231 --> 00:38:22.290
I'm a superstar, and I got a cool car


00:38:22.433 --> 00:38:25.425
And the girls like me better
Than whoever you are


00:38:25.569 --> 00:38:27.764
'Cause I make your day
Let me hear you say


00:38:27.905 --> 00:38:30.965
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh


00:38:32.510 --> 00:38:34.603
Can you give me some of that?


00:38:37.048 --> 00:38:38.413
It's the Crush.


00:38:44.555 --> 00:38:46.750
Here we go, here we go
And the crowd goes


00:38:46.891 --> 00:38:49.121
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh


00:38:49.260 --> 00:38:50.955
Oh, oh, oh, oh


00:38:51.095 --> 00:38:54.656
And the crowd goes
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh


00:38:54.799 --> 00:38:56.164
- Oh, oh, oh, oh
- Come on. What?


00:38:56.300 --> 00:38:59.701
And the crowd goes
I'm a superstar, and I got a cool car


00:38:59.837 --> 00:39:02.499
And the girls like me better
Than whoever you are


00:39:02.640 --> 00:39:05.234
'Cause I make your day
Let me hear you say


00:39:05.376 --> 00:39:08.470
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh


00:39:11.849 --> 00:39:16.252
We're Mudslide Crush.
Thank you for coming out. Whoo!


00:39:29.367 --> 00:39:31.562
What's going on?


00:39:33.437 --> 00:39:37.601
Mudslide Crush.
They're mad we cut their show short.


00:39:37.742 --> 00:39:40.540
- So?
- So they're the cool guys.


00:39:40.678 --> 00:39:42.543
The pride of Mesa High.


00:39:42.680 --> 00:39:47.982
- And what are we?
- We are rash-like, persistent.


00:39:48.119 --> 00:39:49.177
Hmm.


00:39:49.320 --> 00:39:51.811
- Excellent.
- After you.


00:39:53.557 --> 00:39:54.922
- Look at you.
- Yesterday.


00:39:55.059 --> 00:39:56.492
- Oh, okay.
- Yeah.


00:39:56.627 --> 00:39:58.925
I see everyone brought their official
underworld badges.


00:39:59.063 --> 00:40:00.496
- Yeah.
- Yeah.


00:40:00.631 --> 00:40:03.099
- We're subterranean and we're proud.
- Ha, ha.


00:40:03.234 --> 00:40:04.394
- Yeah.
- Mm-hm.


00:40:09.173 --> 00:40:10.697
Ew.


00:40:10.841 --> 00:40:14.709
All right. First order of business:
a band name.


00:40:14.845 --> 00:40:16.369
- We need one for the fliers.
- Right.


00:40:16.514 --> 00:40:18.414
Okay, okay. What about Soul Groove?


00:40:18.549 --> 00:40:20.141
- Mm. Mm-mm.
- No. Oh.


00:40:20.284 --> 00:40:23.117
- Um... The Anarchists?
- No.


00:40:23.254 --> 00:40:25.051
- Well, that's not so bad.
- The Anarchists.


00:40:25.189 --> 00:40:27.350
- No.
- No.


00:40:27.658 --> 00:40:29.125
No, no, you're right, it's terrible.


00:40:29.593 --> 00:40:32.357
Um, I'm gonna go get another lemonade.


00:40:32.496 --> 00:40:33.929
All right, look, guys, I got one.


00:40:34.064 --> 00:40:37.227
Um, let me just find it.


00:40:38.035 --> 00:40:39.195
Oh.


00:40:39.904 --> 00:40:41.838
- Wen.
- Wen?


00:40:41.972 --> 00:40:43.530
- He's kidding, right?
- Come on.


00:40:43.674 --> 00:40:47.633
It's the whole one-name thing.
You know, like, um... Mm.


00:40:47.778 --> 00:40:49.268
- Like Bon Jovi.
- Mm.


00:40:50.047 --> 00:40:51.275
- Or Cher.
- Ha, ha.


00:40:51.415 --> 00:40:53.542
Back off the bash.


00:40:55.186 --> 00:40:57.381
- What kind of band name is that?
- I love it.


00:40:57.521 --> 00:40:59.580
No, this was on the door.


00:41:04.261 --> 00:41:07.128
Good morning.
Over the weekend, I was notified


00:41:07.264 --> 00:41:12.395
that there was gum found underneath the
seats of the new bleachers in the gym.


00:41:13.571 --> 00:41:15.732
This is a personal affront to me.


00:41:15.873 --> 00:41:17.397
I've assigned seven students as our...


00:41:17.541 --> 00:41:18.838
You haven't called me back.


00:41:19.677 --> 00:41:22.475
Sorry. You know,
I've just been distracted.


00:41:22.613 --> 00:41:25.776
Got band rehearsals, soccer practice.


00:41:26.750 --> 00:41:28.980
I mean, you know how it is, right?


00:41:31.088 --> 00:41:34.489
Okay, is that what this is about?
The band?


00:41:34.625 --> 00:41:37.116
- No, no.
- That is all.


00:41:38.062 --> 00:41:41.657
You know, I gotta go.
I'll call you, all right?


00:41:43.968 --> 00:41:45.902
Sure you will.


00:41:55.679 --> 00:42:00.343
If a guy doesn't call for a few days,
should the girl worry?


00:42:01.418 --> 00:42:03.579
Do guys do that?


00:42:03.787 --> 00:42:04.845
You're a guy, right?


00:42:05.289 --> 00:42:07.052
Heh. Wow.


00:42:07.191 --> 00:42:10.718
No, I just mean, like, you're my friend.
You're not, like, a "guy" guy.


00:42:11.795 --> 00:42:13.319
Yeah, that's not really helping.


00:42:13.464 --> 00:42:16.627
What's up. Am I interrupting?


00:42:22.573 --> 00:42:25.007
- Thanks. My favorite.
- Could I just have--?


00:42:25.142 --> 00:42:27.508
So hey, you're the lead singer
of the new band, right?


00:42:27.645 --> 00:42:28.703
Yeah.


00:42:28.846 --> 00:42:30.905
Oh, then why don't you just
belt one out for us?


00:42:31.048 --> 00:42:33.573
- Show us what you've got.
- Could you just leave me alone?


00:42:33.717 --> 00:42:37.244
- What's going on?
- We're just making small talk.


00:42:37.388 --> 00:42:40.255
Ray, come on, bro.
Just leave her alone.


00:42:40.691 --> 00:42:43.023
- And are you gonna make me?
- You're being a creep, Ray.


00:42:45.129 --> 00:42:47.620
So if you're not gonna make me,
then who's gonna make me?


00:42:47.765 --> 00:42:49.130
Me.


00:42:49.800 --> 00:42:51.392
- That's who.
- You?


00:42:51.535 --> 00:42:52.593
- Yeah.
- Yeah?


00:42:52.736 --> 00:42:54.135
- Yeah.
- Yeah, okay.


00:42:54.271 --> 00:42:57.206
- Can't--? Can't we talk this through?
- No, we can't talk it through, no.


00:42:57.341 --> 00:42:58.968
- Wen? Wen?
- Wen.


00:42:59.109 --> 00:43:02.010
- Yeah?
- A little help here, please.


00:43:02.613 --> 00:43:05.207
- No, no, I'm a lover, not a fighter, bro.
- Perfect.


00:43:05.349 --> 00:43:06.816
- Yeah, yeah.
- Go help him.


00:43:06.951 --> 00:43:09.112
- Can you just make it quick?
- Make it quick? Yeah.


00:43:09.253 --> 00:43:10.948
I have a better idea.


00:43:11.288 --> 00:43:13.620
- What?
- One second.


00:43:15.593 --> 00:43:16.787
- Unh!
- Whoa!


00:43:20.731 --> 00:43:24.724
- You think it's funny? Is that what it is?
- No, it's not funny. I'm sorry.


00:43:24.868 --> 00:43:26.733
- You're cra-- No. No, no, no.
- Back off.


00:43:26.870 --> 00:43:29.430
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.
- Guys, stop it.


00:43:29.573 --> 00:43:31.598
Break it up here, break it up.


00:43:31.742 --> 00:43:34.870
Step away from the puddle, people.
What is going on here?


00:43:35.012 --> 00:43:37.947
Principal Brenigan,
I went to go get a TurboBlast,


00:43:38.082 --> 00:43:40.073
and they just start threatening me.


00:43:40.217 --> 00:43:43.380
Next thing you know it,
lemonade mouth over here


00:43:43.520 --> 00:43:45.454
spits all over me.


00:43:48.058 --> 00:43:49.787
Look at my clothes.


00:43:52.529 --> 00:43:53.587
We didn't do anything.


00:43:53.731 --> 00:43:58.225
And that is how we got our band name.


00:44:11.048 --> 00:44:12.276
Hey.


00:44:13.150 --> 00:44:14.777
- What are you doing here?
- Uh...


00:44:14.918 --> 00:44:18.786
Stella said I should come by,
work on some songs with you.


00:44:20.090 --> 00:44:21.352
Oh.


00:44:21.492 --> 00:44:22.959
Okay.


00:44:25.396 --> 00:44:26.988
So, uh...


00:44:27.564 --> 00:44:30.328
Oh, right. Sorry. Um...


00:44:32.302 --> 00:44:33.963
Come on in.


00:44:34.438 --> 00:44:36.531
All right. Oh, wow.


00:44:37.741 --> 00:44:40.141
- Thanks, Gram.
- Mm-hm.


00:44:40.978 --> 00:44:43.913
So you're Olivia's friend?


00:44:45.649 --> 00:44:46.775
That's right.


00:44:46.917 --> 00:44:48.748
I've never met
one of Olivia's friends before.


00:44:48.886 --> 00:44:51.946
- Um... Gram, mm-mm.
- Hmm?


00:44:54.024 --> 00:44:56.458
She was just kidding
about the whole friend thing.


00:44:56.593 --> 00:44:59.892
She's met a ton of my friends.
Like, tons and tons.


00:45:01.331 --> 00:45:03.322
- Friends.
- Right.


00:45:03.467 --> 00:45:04.627
Of course.


00:45:05.302 --> 00:45:06.633
- You wanna hear a rap?
- Oh, yes.


00:45:06.770 --> 00:45:09.295
- Yeah? All right. Um...
- Okay.


00:45:09.440 --> 00:45:11.567
It's Wen, and I'm musically inclined


00:45:11.709 --> 00:45:13.870
Get a shiver down your spine
Every time I rhyme


00:45:14.011 --> 00:45:16.241
I'm in Lemonade Mouth
We don't learn to wait


00:45:16.380 --> 00:45:18.439
We get on stage and determinate


00:45:19.783 --> 00:45:20.875
- Determin--
- Ha, ha.


00:45:21.018 --> 00:45:23.111
- Like, it would keep going.
- Wait, "determinate"?


00:45:23.253 --> 00:45:26.154
Yeah. It's like, get determined.


00:45:26.290 --> 00:45:28.554
- Ha, ha.
- Like, put on your game face. Yes.


00:45:28.926 --> 00:45:32.726
Oh, I'm sorry.
That is so not what "determinate" means.


00:45:34.398 --> 00:45:37.925
Wow. That is an old cat.


00:45:44.174 --> 00:45:45.835
Yeah.


00:45:46.310 --> 00:45:48.608
Yeah, she's really old.


00:45:49.913 --> 00:45:51.278
Are you okay?


00:45:53.851 --> 00:45:55.443
Yeah. Um...


00:45:58.088 --> 00:46:00.921
Nancy was my mom's,
and so she's just kind of like


00:46:01.058 --> 00:46:04.721
the last real thing I have left of her, so...


00:46:06.463 --> 00:46:08.260
Oh, I'm sorry.


00:46:10.300 --> 00:46:12.200
Well, what about your dad?


00:46:14.638 --> 00:46:16.105
He...


00:46:17.007 --> 00:46:18.474
Um...


00:46:18.609 --> 00:46:20.634
You know, can we just
work on the songs?


00:46:20.778 --> 00:46:21.938
Yeah.


00:46:22.079 --> 00:46:25.412
Because I-- I have this one
that I think is pretty good.


00:46:25.549 --> 00:46:27.073
Uh-oh.


00:46:27.217 --> 00:46:29.947
So, um, here.


00:46:31.288 --> 00:46:32.983
Okay.


00:46:34.158 --> 00:46:35.625
Right.


00:46:36.160 --> 00:46:38.253
- And then...
- Okay.


00:46:38.595 --> 00:46:42.224
Trying hard to fight these tears


00:46:42.366 --> 00:46:45.392
I'm crazy worried


00:46:45.536 --> 00:46:49.267
Messing with my head, this fear


00:46:49.406 --> 00:46:52.034
I'm so sorry


00:46:52.176 --> 00:46:55.942
You know you gotta get it out


00:46:56.079 --> 00:46:59.014
I can take it


00:46:59.149 --> 00:47:03.176
That's what being a friend's about


00:47:11.795 --> 00:47:13.922
I like when you smile.


00:47:15.432 --> 00:47:19.061
- Ha, ha. Sorry, I--
- No, it, um...


00:47:19.870 --> 00:47:22.134
- Right, so--
- Yeah, we should... Ahem.


00:47:22.272 --> 00:47:24.536
Basically, it just picks up a little bit


00:47:24.675 --> 00:47:27.143
and we go through, like,
this slow portion of the song, right?


00:47:27.277 --> 00:47:29.370
And then I was thinking that...


00:47:30.414 --> 00:47:34.043
- Well, this is it, guys. Our last rehearsal.
- Lyle.


00:47:35.819 --> 00:47:38.515
Guys, I can't believe
the Halloween Bash is tomorrow night.


00:47:38.655 --> 00:47:41.488
And Rising Star in a few weeks.


00:47:45.829 --> 00:47:46.989
You okay?


00:47:47.831 --> 00:47:50.527
Fine, fine. I'm totally fine.


00:47:51.702 --> 00:47:54.034
- We're all nervous, Olivia.
- Try terrified.


00:47:55.038 --> 00:47:58.872
Hey, come on, you guys,
we're gonna be great.


00:47:59.843 --> 00:48:03.836
In fact, I think I know just the thing
to make us feel better.


00:48:05.182 --> 00:48:06.877
Lemonade.


00:48:11.521 --> 00:48:14.456
I'd like to know what's happening to
the lemonade machine in the basement.


00:48:14.591 --> 00:48:16.821
There's a lemonade machine down there?


00:48:17.494 --> 00:48:20.088
Yeah, for now.


00:48:21.231 --> 00:48:23.665
And I'd like to know
why it's being removed.


00:48:23.800 --> 00:48:25.495
- Oh...
- Hey, we--


00:48:25.636 --> 00:48:29.072
We were just wondering
if it's gonna be replaced or repaired.


00:48:29.206 --> 00:48:33.074
You know, any information you have, we--
We would really appreciate it.


00:48:33.210 --> 00:48:36.077
Well, I'm sure it's just a mix-up.


00:48:36.813 --> 00:48:39.247
See? Just relax.


00:48:44.154 --> 00:48:46.384
Uh-huh. Oh.


00:48:46.657 --> 00:48:48.124
Oh, well.


00:48:48.258 --> 00:48:51.523
Well, that machine
should have been gone ages ago.


00:48:52.229 --> 00:48:54.697
Well, what with Principal Brenigan's
sponsorship deal.


00:48:55.632 --> 00:48:56.963
A sponsorship?


00:48:57.467 --> 00:49:00.368
TurboBlast donated the gym
and the scoreboard,


00:49:00.504 --> 00:49:04.406
and we have to get rid
of any competing drink machines. Ha, ha.


00:49:04.541 --> 00:49:08.477
What? That's the stupidest thing
I've ever heard.


00:49:08.612 --> 00:49:11.080
Now, I don't care for your tone,
young lady.


00:49:11.214 --> 00:49:13.375
I suggest if you have
any more questions,


00:49:13.951 --> 00:49:17.284
you bring them up
to Principal Brenigan yourself.


00:49:17.421 --> 00:49:18.820
It's okay. Relax.


00:49:19.423 --> 00:49:21.618
Yeah, so like I was saying, Maureen,


00:49:21.758 --> 00:49:23.988
he told me I looked nice
and he smiled at me. Ha, ha.


00:49:24.127 --> 00:49:25.651
We're not going down without a fight.


00:49:25.796 --> 00:49:28.629
Ahh. Look, it's just a machine, Stella.


00:49:28.765 --> 00:49:32.223
No, it's not. It's more than that.


00:49:32.369 --> 00:49:35.805
Afternoon, students.
Are we having a good day?


00:49:35.939 --> 00:49:38.772
- Yeah.
- Thank you, Faye.


00:49:55.292 --> 00:49:56.759
Hey there, buddy. You're home early.


00:49:56.893 --> 00:49:59.794
Yeah, practice sort of got cancelled.


00:50:00.664 --> 00:50:02.359
What's all this?


00:50:07.704 --> 00:50:09.467
Sydney's stuff.


00:50:16.980 --> 00:50:18.811
Um, what's it doing here?


00:50:23.487 --> 00:50:27.218
Look, I know
this has been tough for you.


00:50:27.357 --> 00:50:29.985
Mom leaving, me moving on.


00:50:30.127 --> 00:50:33.688
But whatever issues you're having
with Sydney, we have to figure them out,


00:50:33.830 --> 00:50:35.525
because she makes me happy, Wen.


00:50:35.665 --> 00:50:38.896
- Yeah.
- And I've asked her to marry me.


00:50:46.209 --> 00:50:47.801
Wen.


00:50:56.019 --> 00:50:57.919
- Here you go.
- Oh, thank you.


00:50:58.055 --> 00:50:59.818
Hey, Mo.


00:51:00.290 --> 00:51:01.552
What's up with you?


00:51:01.691 --> 00:51:04.717
Nothing. Hey, have you seen
the new weight room?


00:51:04.861 --> 00:51:08.024
- What?
- Oh, okay. You gotta check it out.


00:51:08.165 --> 00:51:09.996
- It's really great.
- Okay.


00:51:10.133 --> 00:51:12.465
So how's that whole band thing
working out for you, anyway?


00:51:12.602 --> 00:51:13.864
Yeah, it's great. Um...


00:51:14.004 --> 00:51:16.529
- What are you up to?
- Can you tell I've been working out?


00:51:16.673 --> 00:51:19.005
Seriously,
I don't have time for your games.


00:51:24.548 --> 00:51:26.516
Hey, Mo. You know Jules, right?


00:51:28.385 --> 00:51:29.545
No, wait, Mo.


00:51:29.886 --> 00:51:31.911
Let her go. Whoa. She's made her choice.


00:51:32.055 --> 00:51:34.455
Hey, good luck tonight.


00:51:43.633 --> 00:51:45.828
Yeah. What's up, man?


00:51:48.138 --> 00:51:49.901
Show 'em all why


00:51:50.040 --> 00:51:51.803
She promised she'd be here.


00:51:52.175 --> 00:51:55.508
- Maybe she just got held up.
- We're on in ten minutes.


00:51:55.645 --> 00:51:57.476
Oh. Guys,


00:51:59.416 --> 00:52:00.747
I can't find her anywhere.


00:52:03.854 --> 00:52:07.722
I don't have time. Those Mudslide jerks
wrecked my setup before sound check.


00:52:07.858 --> 00:52:09.485
I'm telling you, it's sabotage.


00:52:09.860 --> 00:52:12.488
Doesn't matter. We can't go on
