01:09:18.621 --> 01:09:21.146
'Cause she


01:09:21.290 --> 01:09:23.087
She's so gone


01:09:26.862 --> 01:09:30.559
So long. She's so gone


01:09:44.146 --> 01:09:46.979
Lemonade Mouth
was officially a sensation.


01:09:47.116 --> 01:09:48.413
Will you autograph my CD?


01:09:48.551 --> 01:09:52.043
And five strangers
were suddenly much, much more.


01:09:52.488 --> 01:09:53.546
We were friends.


01:09:53.689 --> 01:09:56.055
Can I get your autograph?


01:09:57.259 --> 01:10:00.695
- Would you listen to my demo?
- Charlie!


01:10:14.210 --> 01:10:17.611
What's up, guys?
Has anyone seen Olivia today?


01:10:17.746 --> 01:10:19.680
- I haven't seen her all day.
- No?


01:10:33.362 --> 01:10:35.262
You okay?


01:10:36.665 --> 01:10:38.633
Yeah, you came.


01:10:38.767 --> 01:10:40.598
We all did.


01:10:41.136 --> 01:10:43.969
- Hey.
- Hey, Olivia.


01:10:46.275 --> 01:10:49.870
Look, I'm-- I'm really sorry about Nancy.


01:10:50.546 --> 01:10:52.514
Yeah, me too.


01:10:53.415 --> 01:10:56.942
Hey, it's nice out here.


01:10:59.021 --> 01:11:04.926
Yeah. Sometimes I like to look up
and see what shapes I can find.


01:11:05.060 --> 01:11:07.028
You know, in the clouds.


01:11:07.229 --> 01:11:11.063
It's a giant old lady with a...


01:11:11.400 --> 01:11:13.300
A skirt and an umbrella.


01:11:13.435 --> 01:11:17.565
See, there... There's a flower in a vase.


01:11:19.408 --> 01:11:21.569
Oh, I see a hand.


01:11:21.944 --> 01:11:24.640
No, you're way off. It's a...


01:11:25.080 --> 01:11:29.016
It's a alien pushing a baby carriage.


01:11:32.254 --> 01:11:33.744
All I see is a blob.


01:11:35.958 --> 01:11:39.121
Sometimes I think I'm too stupid
to be in my family.


01:11:40.763 --> 01:11:43.698
Like I'm just some big letdown.


01:11:46.101 --> 01:11:48.899
No wonder my mom ignores me.


01:11:50.072 --> 01:11:52.802
I wish my dad would ignore me.


01:11:54.143 --> 01:11:55.638
I'm never gonna live up to this idea he has


01:11:55.639 --> 01:11:57.772
of this perfect Indian daughter, you know?


01:11:57.913 --> 01:12:00.473
Heh. Try living up to a perfect brother.


01:12:02.251 --> 01:12:07.188
I'd take perfect brother any day
over my dad's ridiculous girlfriend.


01:12:07.589 --> 01:12:09.022
My dad's in prison.


01:12:16.231 --> 01:12:17.596
Ugh.


01:12:18.734 --> 01:12:20.497
I just--


01:12:20.636 --> 01:12:25.164
I'm too humiliated to talk to him
or about him and...


01:12:26.875 --> 01:12:30.174
You know, he writes,
but I don't write back,


01:12:30.746 --> 01:12:33.010
because I don't know what to say.


01:12:34.616 --> 01:12:38.347
I mean, he's made some really bad
decisions since my mom died,


01:12:39.021 --> 01:12:41.353
and I still love him, but he's--


01:12:41.490 --> 01:12:43.481
He's a stranger now, you know?


01:12:45.594 --> 01:12:48.893
Which is why I'm so glad to have this,
you know.


01:12:49.031 --> 01:12:50.896
- Our friendship.
- Mm.


01:12:51.100 --> 01:12:54.467
Yeah. Okay.


01:13:03.045 --> 01:13:07.414
I can't pretend to know how you feel


01:13:07.549 --> 01:13:12.145
But know that I'm here
Know that I'm real


01:13:12.287 --> 01:13:16.656
Say what you want
Or don't talk at all


01:13:16.792 --> 01:13:21.320
Not gonna let you fall


01:13:21.463 --> 01:13:26.059
Reach for my hand
'Cause it's held out for you


01:13:26.201 --> 01:13:30.661
My shoulders are small
But you can cry on them too


01:13:30.806 --> 01:13:37.439
Everything changes
But one thing is true, understand


01:13:37.579 --> 01:13:42.573
We'll always be more than a band


01:13:43.886 --> 01:13:47.982
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah


01:13:49.191 --> 01:13:53.685
You used to brave the world
All on your own


01:13:53.829 --> 01:13:58.061
Now we won't let you go. Go it alone


01:13:58.534 --> 01:14:03.028
Be who you wanna be
Always stand tall


01:14:03.172 --> 01:14:07.575
Not gonna let you fall


01:14:07.709 --> 01:14:12.112
Reach for my hand
'Cause it's held out for you


01:14:12.247 --> 01:14:17.048
My shoulders are strong
But you can cry on them too


01:14:17.186 --> 01:14:22.886
Everything changes
But one thing is true, understand


01:14:23.792 --> 01:14:26.522
We'll always be more than a band


01:14:26.662 --> 01:14:30.962
I never knew you could take me so far


01:14:31.099 --> 01:14:34.591
I've always wanted the hope


01:14:34.736 --> 01:14:44.168
- That you are the ones I need
- Yeah


01:14:44.913 --> 01:14:49.043
Reach for my hand
'Cause it's held out for you


01:14:49.184 --> 01:14:53.780
My shoulders are strong
But you can cry on them too


01:14:53.922 --> 01:15:00.623
Everything changes
But one thing is true, understand


01:15:00.762 --> 01:15:03.162
We'll always be more than a band


01:15:03.298 --> 01:15:07.496
Reach for my hand
'Cause it's held out for you


01:15:07.636 --> 01:15:12.335
My shoulders are strong
But you can cry on them too


01:15:12.474 --> 01:15:19.073
Everything changes
But one thing is true, understand


01:15:19.214 --> 01:15:25.847
We'll always be more than a band


01:15:30.959 --> 01:15:32.324
Hey.


01:15:32.895 --> 01:15:34.522
Oh, come on, Mo.


01:15:34.663 --> 01:15:35.789
Can we please just talk?


01:15:35.931 --> 01:15:38.263
- We don't have anything to talk about.
- I think we do.


01:15:38.400 --> 01:15:40.334
Look, Mo, I made a mistake.


01:15:44.673 --> 01:15:46.106
Look, Mo.


01:15:47.776 --> 01:15:49.710
l still have feelings for you.


01:15:51.346 --> 01:15:52.404
What about Jules?


01:15:52.814 --> 01:15:55.578
Mo, come on, we're just friends.
That's all.


01:15:58.020 --> 01:16:00.147
The thing is, Scott,


01:16:01.523 --> 01:16:04.048
I'm not the same girl I was
two months ago.


01:16:05.694 --> 01:16:09.858
Not anymore. I'm not trying to be
something that I'm not, you know?


01:16:10.399 --> 01:16:11.525
Not for anyone.


01:16:13.235 --> 01:16:16.602
Me, my music,
we're a package deal now.


01:16:16.738 --> 01:16:19.673
Okay, and I know. I get that now, I do.


01:16:21.577 --> 01:16:25.377
And I'm sorry, Mo. I am.


01:16:26.148 --> 01:16:27.615
Just...


01:16:28.784 --> 01:16:30.251
Can you forgive me?


01:16:33.288 --> 01:16:34.380
Of course I can.


01:16:36.992 --> 01:16:39.927
But it doesn't change anything
between us.


01:16:40.062 --> 01:16:41.461
Okay?


01:16:43.131 --> 01:16:45.861
It's gonna take a lot more than "sorry"
to fix this.


01:16:47.002 --> 01:16:50.301
Come on, Mo, just wait. Mo.


01:16:53.675 --> 01:16:55.768
The band was, uh... Ha, ha.


01:16:55.911 --> 01:16:58.880
Was originally called Wen.


01:16:59.014 --> 01:17:02.814
And, I know, but after about
months and months of arguing, uh,


01:17:02.951 --> 01:17:04.418
- and debating the--
- Wen.


01:17:04.553 --> 01:17:05.815
- Don't you knock?
- Yes.


01:17:05.954 --> 01:17:09.219
No. Just-- Come on.
You've got to hear this.


01:17:09.925 --> 01:17:12.985
I can't deny
Tonight I wanna up and hide


01:17:13.128 --> 01:17:16.154
- Listen. Your song.
- And get inside


01:17:16.298 --> 01:17:18.095
- It's you. Ha, ha.
- What?


01:17:18.233 --> 01:17:19.962
Yes. Ha-ha-ha.


01:17:20.102 --> 01:17:22.502
- Yes! What?
- It's you.


01:17:22.638 --> 01:17:24.606
- That's incredible.
- What's going on?


01:17:24.740 --> 01:17:27.174
- We're on the radio.
- Ha-ha-ha.


01:17:34.483 --> 01:17:37.941
- Hello?
- Turn on WRIZ.


01:17:48.196 --> 01:17:51.165
I gotta get myself on-stage


01:17:51.299 --> 01:17:52.357
I shouldn't wait


01:17:52.501 --> 01:17:54.628
Gram. Gram. They're playing our song.


01:17:54.936 --> 01:17:57.131
On the radio.
They're playing our song on the radio!


01:17:57.272 --> 01:17:58.603
Yes! Yes!


01:18:01.777 --> 01:18:05.110
The radio sponsor for Rising Star
heard our demo and put it on the air.


01:18:05.247 --> 01:18:07.807
It was a dream come true. For all of us.


01:18:07.949 --> 01:18:10.008
Like there's lemons in their mouth


01:18:10.152 --> 01:18:11.619
I'm the real deal
You know how I feel


01:18:11.753 --> 01:18:13.380
We're not in it for the mill
We're just in it for a thrill


01:18:13.522 --> 01:18:14.921
Get down now
I ain't playin' around


01:18:15.057 --> 01:18:16.718
Put your feet up on the ground
And just make that sound


01:18:16.858 --> 01:18:20.692
But just when the future
looked brightest for Lemonade Mouth,


01:18:20.829 --> 01:18:22.956
everything started to fall apart.


01:18:26.401 --> 01:18:29.199
Set free what is inside of me


01:18:33.408 --> 01:18:35.376
Mo, you sure you're okay?


01:18:35.510 --> 01:18:36.875
Yeah, I think it's just allergies.


01:18:37.012 --> 01:18:38.912
It's a long way down, but I say


01:18:39.047 --> 01:18:41.709
Oh, we're gonna let it show


01:18:42.484 --> 01:18:43.815
- We're gonna
- Losers.


01:18:45.520 --> 01:18:48.751
I'm just saying, I'm gonna take you down
at Rising Star tomorrow. You just wait.


01:18:49.491 --> 01:18:51.789
Look, just ignore him.


01:18:52.427 --> 01:18:54.691
--back our dreams and try--


01:18:55.697 --> 01:18:58.359
All right, thanks.
Hey, good evening, ladies and gentlemen.


01:18:58.500 --> 01:19:01.333
May I introduce Loser Mouth--?


01:19:01.470 --> 01:19:03.836
- Give me the-- Give me the mic--
- No, no, bro.


01:19:05.307 --> 01:19:07.639
Hey. Oh!


01:19:08.977 --> 01:19:10.342
Whoa!


01:19:13.482 --> 01:19:14.949
We wanna party


01:19:15.083 --> 01:19:16.380
So get started


01:19:18.019 --> 01:19:19.077
We wanna rock it


01:19:19.454 --> 01:19:21.251
Calm down.


01:19:24.092 --> 01:19:26.083
Go, go, go


01:19:27.496 --> 01:19:29.293
Go, go, go


01:19:29.431 --> 01:19:30.728
Yeah, yeah


01:19:34.002 --> 01:19:36.493
Yeah. Yeah.


01:19:36.638 --> 01:19:40.665
- Ooh! Uh-oh.
- Oh!


01:19:42.144 --> 01:19:44.704
- Ray is such a jerk.
- He got what he wanted, didn't he?


01:19:44.846 --> 01:19:47.713
Dante's not gonna let us
play there anymore, that's for sure.


01:19:51.119 --> 01:19:52.381
You sure you're okay?


01:19:52.888 --> 01:19:55.823
Yeah, I'm fine.
Just a little bit tired, that's all.


01:19:56.191 --> 01:19:57.920
Wait, wait, Mo.


01:19:58.894 --> 01:20:02.990
There's, um,
something I need to tell you.


01:20:04.633 --> 01:20:06.931
For a long time, I've wanted to
tell you, just, you were--


01:20:07.068 --> 01:20:11.232
You were with Scott,
and then we became friends...


01:20:13.074 --> 01:20:16.771
I like you, Mo. There, I said it.


01:20:19.147 --> 01:20:22.446
We're just friends, Charlie.
Good friends. That's all.


01:20:22.584 --> 01:20:24.643
- Fine.
- Charlie, please, just--


01:20:24.786 --> 01:20:26.253
No, you know what?


01:20:26.788 --> 01:20:30.849
"Be heard"? It's a stupid song.


01:20:30.992 --> 01:20:32.653
- What?
- I'm never singing it again.


01:20:32.794 --> 01:20:36.355
No, Charlie, no. Don't go.


01:20:37.666 --> 01:20:38.826
It's time to come in, Monu.


01:20:44.239 --> 01:20:46.799
You are too young for boys.


01:20:46.942 --> 01:20:49.206
Charlie is just a friend, Baba.


01:20:49.344 --> 01:20:52.006
I didn't come to this country
and make the sacrifices I made


01:20:52.147 --> 01:20:55.344
just so that you can
throw it all away on boys.


01:20:55.483 --> 01:20:56.950
And rock bands.


01:20:57.085 --> 01:21:00.077
Charlie is just a friend, okay?


01:21:01.389 --> 01:21:03.357
And the band?


01:21:07.462 --> 01:21:10.454
It's nothing.
It's just a bit of fun, that's all.


01:21:10.599 --> 01:21:11.827
What's going on?


01:21:14.569 --> 01:21:15.866
Baba doesn't trust me.


01:21:17.172 --> 01:21:18.730
We do trust you, Monu.


01:21:20.675 --> 01:21:22.142
Do you?


01:21:28.617 --> 01:21:32.018
- That's what I thought.
- Mohini?


01:21:32.153 --> 01:21:33.745
Hey.


01:21:34.322 --> 01:21:36.449
You're burning up.


01:21:36.958 --> 01:21:39.188
Let's get you to bed.


01:22:00.415 --> 01:22:01.780
Ow!


01:22:05.220 --> 01:22:06.380
Ow.


01:22:06.521 --> 01:22:09.217
A little to the right. Right, no, left.


01:22:09.357 --> 01:22:11.291
- There. Good.
- Unh.


01:22:11.426 --> 01:22:14.395
Yeah. Thanks for helping.
It'll mean a lot to Sydney.


01:22:14.529 --> 01:22:16.690
- You got it.
- So, Wen,


01:22:16.831 --> 01:22:19.265
- Yeah?
- I've been meaning to ask you.


01:22:20.702 --> 01:22:22.226
Will you be my best man?


01:22:23.405 --> 01:22:24.463
Your what?


01:22:27.342 --> 01:22:30.834
Wen, you okay? Let me see.


01:22:31.680 --> 01:22:35.377
Mo has a hundred-and-two fever,
Charlie has three broken fingers.


01:22:35.517 --> 01:22:37.382
Tomorrow's gonna be a disaster.


01:22:37.519 --> 01:22:39.316
Well, we'll just call and back out.


01:22:39.454 --> 01:22:42.446
No. Back out of Rising Star?
Out of everything we've been through?


01:22:42.590 --> 01:22:43.750
Whoa.


01:22:44.726 --> 01:22:45.818
You okay?


01:22:46.328 --> 01:22:48.228
Yeah. Yeah, I just--


01:22:48.363 --> 01:22:50.763
I just get blurry vision sometimes.


01:22:50.899 --> 01:22:52.730
What do you mean?


01:22:52.867 --> 01:22:54.892
Oh. Wow.


01:22:55.036 --> 01:22:59.097
Yeah. Doctor said
it should be gone in a couple days.


01:22:59.708 --> 01:23:00.766
What happened?


01:23:01.977 --> 01:23:03.672
- Sydney.
- Sydney did it?


01:23:03.812 --> 01:23:07.111
Well, Sydney's picture.
I was helping my dad hang it up,


01:23:07.248 --> 01:23:10.149
and then he asked me to be his best man.


01:23:10.685 --> 01:23:12.744
Wen, that's great news.


01:23:12.887 --> 01:23:15.583
- No. Okay, that's terrible news.
- Oh.


01:23:15.724 --> 01:23:18.557
All right, just because Sydney
wormed her way into my family


01:23:18.693 --> 01:23:20.456
doesn't mean
I have to be happy about it.


01:23:22.063 --> 01:23:24.327
You're-- You're ridiculous.


01:23:27.936 --> 01:23:31.428
Wen. Wait, where are you going?
Hey, we have to talk about tomorrow.


01:23:31.573 --> 01:23:35.509
What's to talk about?
Okay, we can't play. So we're out.


01:23:36.911 --> 01:23:37.969
You know, maybe...


01:23:38.613 --> 01:23:43.016
Maybe this is a sign.
Maybe it's time to call it quits.


01:23:43.318 --> 01:23:45.650
What, so you just wanna give up?


01:23:45.787 --> 01:23:47.414
You just be happy
that you're off the hook


01:23:47.555 --> 01:23:49.750
- and don't have to go on-stage anymore.
- No, no.


01:23:49.891 --> 01:23:51.381
Wen, this isn't about Lemonade Mouth.


01:23:51.526 --> 01:23:54.359
This is about you not appreciating
what you have.


01:23:54.963 --> 01:23:58.660
You have a family.
Your dad, your sister, Sydney.


01:23:58.800 --> 01:24:00.233
I don't even remember my mom.


01:24:00.368 --> 01:24:01.835
I haven't talked to my dad in years,


01:24:01.970 --> 01:24:04.837
and you have the nerve
to feel sorry for yourself?


01:24:05.440 --> 01:24:07.772
Well, okay, no, fine.
Go ahead, give up. See if I care.


01:24:07.909 --> 01:24:10.070
I didn't even wanna be in this band
in the first place.


01:24:10.211 --> 01:24:13.408
- Well, then why did you do it?
- Oh, for you, you jerk!


01:24:17.652 --> 01:24:19.711
I did it for you.


01:24:40.542 --> 01:24:42.373
Hey, it's me.


01:24:42.610 --> 01:24:45.340
We have an emergency.


01:24:45.780 --> 01:24:47.975
I'm right in front of the school.


01:24:48.116 --> 01:24:49.583
Yeah, yeah. Hurry.


01:24:50.919 --> 01:24:53.615
- Anybody know what this is about?
- Where is she?


01:24:53.755 --> 01:24:55.222
What happened to your voice?


01:24:55.457 --> 01:24:56.754
There she is.


01:25:01.262 --> 01:25:03.594
- What happened?
- Achoo.


01:25:03.731 --> 01:25:06.222
Did you all get hit
by a bus or something?


01:25:06.367 --> 01:25:08.927
- Look who's talking.
- What's going on, Stella?


01:25:09.070 --> 01:25:10.935
Yeah. What are you doing?


01:25:11.673 --> 01:25:16.133
I am protesting the removal
of our Mel's Lemonade machine. Hmm.


01:25:17.512 --> 01:25:19.707
You're kidding me, right?
In this weather?


01:25:19.848 --> 01:25:21.941
Okay, kid, enough playing around.


01:25:22.083 --> 01:25:23.744
I got three more pickups today.


01:25:24.586 --> 01:25:26.213
It's gonna rain. Let's get out of here.


01:25:26.754 --> 01:25:28.722
Are you really willing to support


01:25:30.358 --> 01:25:33.122
the rampant tyranny and oppression
of the powerful over the voiceless?


01:25:33.261 --> 01:25:36.230
- Aw.
- You move, or I move you. It's your choice.


01:25:36.364 --> 01:25:37.592
Humph.


01:25:37.732 --> 01:25:43.796
I am not moving until you put
our lemonade machine back.


01:25:44.572 --> 01:25:46.039
- Have it your way, kid.
- All right.


01:25:46.174 --> 01:25:47.869
- Hey, no.
- Hey. Hey, put her down.


01:25:48.009 --> 01:25:50.102
- Get off of my friend!
- Hey.


01:25:50.311 --> 01:25:51.608
Stop!


01:25:59.053 --> 01:26:03.752
Needless to say, that day
was a bit of a low for the band.


01:26:07.562 --> 01:26:09.359
So much for Rising Star.


01:26:09.497 --> 01:26:11.624
We can't skip it.


01:26:11.766 --> 01:26:14.428
Well, we can't play.


01:26:14.569 --> 01:26:16.196
It's over.


01:26:16.905 --> 01:26:18.031
Wen's right.


01:26:19.340 --> 01:26:20.932
We lose.


01:26:23.378 --> 01:26:27.576
So we lose. So what?


01:26:29.284 --> 01:26:32.151
Lemonade Mouth
is bigger than a competition.


01:26:33.221 --> 01:26:35.212
We did it to be heard.


01:26:35.723 --> 01:26:40.023
For our fans, for ourselves.


01:26:40.161 --> 01:26:42.823
- For our friendship.
- Thank you.


01:26:43.531 --> 01:26:45.590
Guys, we can't give up.


01:26:45.733 --> 01:26:49.125
Olivia, this isn't
just humiliating ourselves on,


01:26:49.126 --> 01:26:50.397
like, a high-school level.


01:26:50.538 --> 01:26:53.234
- Look, we're not doing it.
- Agreed.


01:26:54.642 --> 01:26:58.578
In case you haven't noticed, Stella,
we're in a holding cell.


01:26:59.147 --> 01:27:01.308
Okay, and you're the only one to blame.


01:27:01.716 --> 01:27:03.411
- Me?
- Yeah, you.


01:27:03.551 --> 01:27:05.542
Yeah, it's pretty much
all your fault, Stella.


01:27:07.322 --> 01:27:10.985
We didn't actually get arrested.


01:27:11.125 --> 01:27:13.685
Okay? We're waiting for our parents
to come pick us up.


01:27:13.828 --> 01:27:17.059
Oh. Great. Our parents.


01:27:17.198 --> 01:27:20.656
- Guys, can you please stop fighting?
- Stupid...


01:27:53.935 --> 01:27:56.267
It would be there just like that


01:27:56.404 --> 01:27:59.430
No matter what. We'll still be singing


01:27:59.574 --> 01:28:02.042
Come on, come on, turn up the music


01:28:02.176 --> 01:28:03.666
It's all we got. We're gonna use it


01:28:05.046 --> 01:28:07.037
Come on, come on, turn up the music


01:28:07.181 --> 01:28:09.809
- Are we in?
- Ha, ha. This is crazy.


01:28:11.886 --> 01:28:13.080
Boys.


01:28:13.221 --> 01:28:16.054
- Oh, watch my eye. Ow. Oh.
- I know. Sorry.


01:28:16.190 --> 01:28:17.589
We sent two cars out there now...


01:28:19.327 --> 01:28:21.557
Oh, darling.


01:28:21.863 --> 01:28:26.061
When I said get out of the house,
this isn't what I meant. Ha, ha.


01:28:26.200 --> 01:28:30.193
- Gram.
- Oh, my sweetheart. Oh.


01:28:35.043 --> 01:28:37.671
Wen, your dad,
he's stuck in town at work.


01:28:37.812 --> 01:28:40.576
He's on his way.
I just thought I'd come and--


01:28:43.885 --> 01:28:46.319
- Thanks for coming.
- Absolutely.


01:28:55.897 --> 01:28:58.195
Okay, look, I know
you're disappointed in me, but I just--


01:28:58.333 --> 01:28:59.960
I don't want to talk about it. Let's go.


01:29:00.101 --> 01:29:01.796
No, Baba, please.


01:29:02.470 --> 01:29:04.631
I need to say this.


01:29:08.276 --> 01:29:14.476
Look, I'm never gonna be this perfect
Indian daughter you want me to be.


01:29:15.516 --> 01:29:18.781
I'm never gonna be
just a regular American teenager.


01:29:19.420 --> 01:29:23.686
I guess I don't know what I am exactly,
maybe a little bit of both?


01:29:23.825 --> 01:29:27.352
But what I'm trying to say is,


01:29:29.697 --> 01:29:31.892
I'm finding my way.


01:29:32.100 --> 01:29:34.466
And, yeah, I'll make mistakes.


01:29:36.504 --> 01:29:39.337
But I deserve for you
to just let me be me.


01:29:43.478 --> 01:29:45.639
Could you at least try, Baba?


01:29:51.586 --> 01:29:52.917
But you're still in trouble.


01:29:55.022 --> 01:29:56.546
I know.


01:29:57.859 --> 01:30:00.020
Ahh. Here we go.


01:30:03.164 --> 01:30:04.825
Tommy?


01:30:07.869 --> 01:30:10.269
You're lucky I picked up the phone
instead of Mom.


01:30:10.405 --> 01:30:12.032
Tell me about it.


01:30:12.173 --> 01:30:13.504
Here's the thing, Charlie.


01:30:13.875 --> 01:30:15.240
You wanna play music,


01:30:15.376 --> 01:30:17.844
you need to stand up to Mom and Dad
and tell them that.


01:30:17.979 --> 01:30:20.038
Tell them soccer isn't for you.


01:30:20.181 --> 01:30:25.141
That you wanna go to music school,
not Stanford.


01:30:25.286 --> 01:30:29.780
That's easy for you to say.
They think everything you do is perfect.


01:30:29.924 --> 01:30:32.051
Yeah, well,
they're not thinking that for long.


01:30:34.061 --> 01:30:37.690
My grades this semester? Not so hot.


01:30:39.167 --> 01:30:41.067
So much for that whole
"perfect" thing, huh?


01:30:42.069 --> 01:30:43.798
Here's an idea.


01:30:44.872 --> 01:30:48.103
What do you say we go
tell Mom and Dad together?


01:31:10.431 --> 01:31:12.228
Yeah, I know.


01:31:14.235 --> 01:31:16.294
Grounded for life.


01:31:17.238 --> 01:31:20.765
You got off with a warning.
Let's just leave it at that.


01:31:23.811 --> 01:31:27.076
Do you know what I see
when I look at you, Stella?


01:31:27.215 --> 01:31:33.779
I see the most determined,
focused girl I've ever known.


01:31:33.921 --> 01:31:37.516
I mean, look at what you've done.
You started a band.


01:31:37.658 --> 01:31:40.024
You stood up for what you believed in.


01:31:41.028 --> 01:31:45.328
I'm sorry that I've been
so distracted lately.


01:31:45.867 --> 01:31:47.858
But, Stell,


01:31:50.304 --> 01:31:53.603
I couldn't be any prouder of what I see.


01:31:56.043 --> 01:31:57.101
Really?


01:32:03.851 --> 01:32:07.116
- Thanks, Mom.
- Hey, let's get out of here.


01:32:07.255 --> 01:32:08.449
Okay.


01:32:11.392 --> 01:32:12.825
Hey.


01:32:13.661 --> 01:32:15.458
You wanna come see our revolution?


01:32:15.930 --> 01:32:18.694
We were planning on it.


01:32:18.833 --> 01:32:20.357
"We"?


01:32:24.539 --> 01:32:26.803
You guys, come here.


01:32:30.144 --> 01:32:31.907
Ladies and gentlemen,


01:32:32.046 --> 01:32:34.776
Rising Star presents Mudslide Crush.


01:32:38.452 --> 01:32:40.750
My girl is hotter than your girl


01:32:40.888 --> 01:32:42.822
You know it, you know it


01:32:42.957 --> 01:32:45.425
Yeah, my ride is sweeter than your ride


01:32:45.560 --> 01:32:47.619
You know it, you know it


01:32:47.762 --> 01:32:51.994
Don't you wish you were us?
Don't you wish you were us?


01:32:53.000 --> 01:32:57.334
You know we own this party
You know we run this town


01:32:57.471 --> 01:33:01.840
I'm about to steal your girlfriend
I'm about to knock you down


01:33:01.976 --> 01:33:04.274
Sorry, but your train has left the station


01:33:04.412 --> 01:33:06.710
Maybe you should try
A permanent vacation


01:33:06.847 --> 01:33:11.443
Never even got an invitation
Did ya? Did ya?


01:33:11.586 --> 01:33:16.421
Hey, what?
Don't you wish you were us?


01:33:16.557 --> 01:33:20.721
Hey, what?
Don't you wish you could rock?


01:33:20.861 --> 01:33:23.523
You're MIA. We're VIP


01:33:23.664 --> 01:33:26.132
You're LOL. We're BIG


01:33:26.267 --> 01:33:31.762
No one really likes you that much
Don't you wish you were us?


01:33:31.906 --> 01:33:33.032
Yeah


01:33:34.842 --> 01:33:39.438
Don't you wish you were us?
Yeah, yeah


01:33:40.448 --> 01:33:45.476
Now all the pretty girls are waiting
To get their picture taken


01:33:47.221 --> 01:33:48.916
With the Crush


01:33:49.056 --> 01:33:50.785
Don't you wish you were us?


01:33:53.761 --> 01:33:55.592
Yeah, don't you wish you were us?


01:33:55.730 --> 01:33:59.063
- They really are...
- Very, very good.


01:33:59.200 --> 01:34:04.729
Whoo! Hey, what?
Don't you wish you were us?


01:34:04.872 --> 01:34:09.400
Hey, what?
Don't you wish you could rock?


01:34:09.543 --> 01:34:11.602
You're MIA. We're VIP


01:34:11.746 --> 01:34:14.271
You're LOL. We're BIG


01:34:14.415 --> 01:34:19.648
No one really likes you that much
Don't you wish you were--?


01:34:38.472 --> 01:34:40.201
Top that.


01:34:40.341 --> 01:34:42.866
Oh, we will. Trust me.


01:34:48.983 --> 01:34:51.781
- Good luck.
- Thanks.


01:34:51.919 --> 01:34:54.683
Ladies and gentlemen, Lemonade Mouth.


01:35:26.487 --> 01:35:29.979
Trying hard to fight these tears


01:35:30.124 --> 01:35:32.319
I'm crazy worried


01:35:33.794 --> 01:35:35.523
Messing with my head, this fear


01:35:37.732 --> 01:35:39.097
I'm so sorry.


01:35:42.837 --> 01:35:44.668
In the bag.


01:35:44.805 --> 01:35:47.205
Please. You can do this.


01:35:47.341 --> 01:35:48.603
I can't.


01:35:59.754 --> 01:36:00.812
Olivia.


01:36:24.145 --> 01:36:26.204
- Okay, where are you going?
- They need help, man.


01:36:26.347 --> 01:36:30.113
No, no. You do that, man,
and you're out of the band for good.


01:36:37.358 --> 01:36:41.317
Trying hard to fight these tears


01:36:41.462 --> 01:36:44.158
I'm crazy worried


01:36:44.732 --> 01:36:47.895
Messing with my head, this fear


01:36:48.035 --> 01:36:50.265
I'm so sorry


01:36:50.871 --> 01:36:54.307
You know, you gotta get it out


01:36:54.441 --> 01:36:56.306
I can take it


01:36:57.311 --> 01:36:59.779
That's what being a friend's about


01:37:01.482 --> 01:37:04.645
Then I guess, you know,
I'll find another band.


01:37:04.785 --> 01:37:05.979
Man, don't walk away from me.


01:37:06.620 --> 01:37:07.848
I, I wanna cry


01:37:09.924 --> 01:37:11.357
I can't deny


01:37:11.492 --> 01:37:14.655
Tonight I wanna up and hide


01:37:14.795 --> 01:37:16.490
And get inside


01:37:16.630 --> 01:37:17.995
It isn't right


01:37:18.132 --> 01:37:20.896
I gotta live in my life


01:37:21.035 --> 01:37:24.300
I know I, I know I, I know I gotta do it


01:37:24.438 --> 01:37:27.601
I know I, I know I, I know I gotta do it


01:37:27.741 --> 01:37:31.040
Gotta turn the world
Into your dance floor


01:37:31.178 --> 01:37:34.443
Determinate. Determinate


01:37:34.949 --> 01:37:38.009
Push until you can't
And then demand more


01:37:38.152 --> 01:37:41.053
Determinate. Determinate


01:37:41.188 --> 01:37:44.954
You and me together


01:37:45.092 --> 01:37:48.550
We can make it better


01:37:48.696 --> 01:37:52.063
Gotta turn the world
Into your dance floor


01:37:52.199 --> 01:37:54.793
Determinate. Determinate.


01:37:56.270 --> 01:37:58.238
Yeah!


01:38:07.181 --> 01:38:09.809
We didn't win Rising Star,


01:38:09.950 --> 01:38:13.716
but we won something bigger that night.


01:38:23.831 --> 01:38:26.231
- Hey.
- Hey.


01:38:27.468 --> 01:38:29.026
Thank you for helping us out.


01:38:30.938 --> 01:38:32.565
It's the least I could do.


01:38:40.247 --> 01:38:43.114
So this package deal
that you were talking about?


01:38:43.584 --> 01:38:45.916
- You and your music?
- Yeah?


01:38:46.420 --> 01:38:47.887
Well, it sounds pretty good.


01:38:49.323 --> 01:38:52.850
And if you, um--
If you could give me a chance,


01:38:53.427 --> 01:38:55.918
I'd really like to get to know this Mohini.


01:38:58.198 --> 01:38:59.825
- Yeah.
- Yeah?


01:38:59.967 --> 01:39:01.662
I'd like that.


01:39:13.113 --> 01:39:16.048
- Hey, Charlie.
- Hey.


01:39:16.483 --> 01:39:17.916
Hey.


01:39:35.903 --> 01:39:37.200
- Hey.
- Hey.


01:39:37.338 --> 01:39:41.331
- What's up?
- I brought you something.


01:39:41.475 --> 01:39:45.536
What is it? Oh, my goodness.


01:39:45.679 --> 01:39:48.773
Oh, the little kitty.
Where did you get her?


01:39:48.916 --> 01:39:52.079
One of Sydney's old roommates
found a whole litter,


01:39:52.219 --> 01:39:54.779
and, uh, I thought of you.


01:39:54.922 --> 01:39:57.083
Oh, she's adorable.


01:39:58.425 --> 01:40:01.053
Hi. Hi.


01:40:01.195 --> 01:40:02.628
You were right, you know.


01:40:03.630 --> 01:40:05.291
About Sydney.


01:40:05.866 --> 01:40:11.429
You know, she may not be my mom,
but she definitely cares.


01:40:11.905 --> 01:40:16.899
I mean, it's not perfect, but it's okay.


01:40:17.244 --> 01:40:21.112
Yeah, well, perfect, Wen?
Way overrated.


01:40:21.615 --> 01:40:23.173
Come here.


01:40:24.318 --> 01:40:27.185
Thank you. Thank you.


01:40:27.988 --> 01:40:30.582
For a long time
there has been an empty spot


01:40:30.724 --> 01:40:33.750
in my life and in my heart.


01:40:33.894 --> 01:40:37.386
And meeting you has brought joy
back into my life.


01:40:37.531 --> 01:40:39.965
In life, and in music,


01:40:40.100 --> 01:40:44.196
things have a funny way of turning out
exactly the way they're supposed to.


01:40:44.338 --> 01:40:50.573
--will make Wen and Georgie and I
happy and complete


01:40:50.711 --> 01:40:52.736
for the rest of our lives.


01:40:54.114 --> 01:40:56.014
That's my band mate up there.


01:40:56.150 --> 01:40:58.584
- And that's my old college buddy.
- Huh.


01:40:59.386 --> 01:41:01.946
See, you and me, we're, like,
practically best friends already.


01:41:04.224 --> 01:41:05.885
You know, I used to be in a band too.


01:41:07.194 --> 01:41:10.027
- Really?
- Yeah. Played bass.


01:41:10.831 --> 01:41:11.889
What do you do now?


01:41:12.032 --> 01:41:14.967
Now I own an organic lemonade company.


01:41:15.102 --> 01:41:17.402
Thing is going gangbusters. It's crazy.


01:41:17.426 --> 01:41:19.280
People just can't get enough of the stuff.


01:41:22.376 --> 01:41:25.368
- Mel?
- Yeah.


01:41:31.452 --> 01:41:33.420
Let me ask you something, Mel.


01:41:34.755 --> 01:41:37.280
Sometimes, risking it all
to have your voice heard


01:41:37.424 --> 01:41:39.984
pays off in ways you never imagined.


01:41:40.127 --> 01:41:42.595
Mel understood this,
and was more than happy


01:41:42.729 --> 01:41:46.392
